            "review_title": "Review at Bun Dau A Vung",
            "review_text": "Anh Amắn 🇻🇳\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12939 contributions\n1\n“Tantalizing pork dish in District 1”\nFeb 2018\nA Saigonese friend brought me here for lunch when I asked him to take me to where he would normally go for a special local treat. \n\nIt is mainly sliced pork and pork meatballs etc served with salads and a variety of fresh herbs and accompaniments. It is these accompaniments. that take the whole dinning experience to another level. OMG! The home made fish sauce is the ultimate, mixed into this to flavour you can add as much or as little diced fresh chilli, sugar and something that looks like baby limes but are called something else (??), and are so full of juice. Once you have your base sauce ready you just eat by hand rolling up the pork in lettuce and herbs and dunking into the sauce. As a side there is delicious tofu as well which goes so well with the fish sauce. This is all very simple straight forward eating but the flavours released from the fish sauce and the accompaniments are simply sensational. Writing about it now, just makes my mouth water. I am so going back there in two weeks time when I am In Saigon again.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 14, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
